Arrays2_BoundedMaximum
Success rate: 32.95%
Given an integer array nums and two integers left and right, return the number of contiguous non-empty subarrays such that the value of the maximum array element in that subarray is in the range [left, right].

Input Format:
The first line contains an integer n (length of the array nums).
The second line contains n space-separated integers representing the elements of the array nums.
The third line contains two space-separated integers left and right.

Output Format:
A single integer representing the number of contiguous non-empty subarrays where the value of the maximum 
array element in that subarray is in the range [left, right].

Constraints:
1 <= nums.length <= 105
0 <= nums[i] <= 109
0 <= left <= right <= 109

Sample test cases
Input
5
2 9 2 5 6
2 8
Expected output
7
Input
5
2 1 4 3 5
2 4
Expected output
9

T.C: O(N^3), S.C: O(1)

    static void boundedMax(int[] arr,int left, int right){
	int n = arr.length;
    int count = 0; // This will count the valid subarrays
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
         	for(int j=i;j<n;j++){
            int ans = Integer.MIN_VALUE;//to check if elements lies in the range of left and right.
              	for(int k=i;k<=j;k++){
              	ans = Math.max(arr[k],ans);// Till whatever the element is read which one is the maximum element
              	}
                if(ans>=left && ans<=right){ // Is that maximum lies between the range of left and right,
                  count++;
                }
            }
        }
        System.out.println(count);
    }

